# Godoc

Follow [.cursor/skills/godoc/SKILL.md](../skills/godoc/SKILL.md).

- Every exported `func`, `type`, `const`, `var`, and method needs a godoc comment.
- **Non-negotiable lead name:** the first word/phrase of the comment is the
  declaration name (`// Foo does ...`), not `This`/`The`/`For`/etc. without that
  name. Wrong: `// This function does ...`, `// The Foo type ...` (lead with
  `Foo`, not a detour). Types may use an optional leading article (`// A Foo
  is ...` / `// An Foo ...` / `// The Foo ...`) only when the identifier follows
  immediately.
- Package-level overview goes in `doc.go` when it helps readers.
- CI fails on violations via golangci-lint revive `exported` and staticcheck
  `ST1020`/`ST1021`/`ST1022` (public API). Unexported helpers do not need godoc
  for CI. Fix before CodeRabbit; do not wait for review nits.
- Ignore CodeRabbit private/unexported docstring coverage %; it is not a gate
  and must not drive PR changes.

Browse locally: `go doc github.com/sviatsviatsviat/wat/<package>`
